problem:
The graph of \( y = \frac{p(x)}{q(x)} \) is shown below, where \( p(x) \) and \( q(x) \) are quadratic. Assume that the grid lines are at integers.

[asy]
unitsize(0.6 cm);

real func (real x) {
  return (3*(x - 2)/(x + 3));
}

int i;

for (i = -8; i <= 8; ++i) {
  draw((i,-8)--(i,8),gray(0.7));
  draw((-8,i)--(8,i),gray(0.7));
}

draw((-8,0)--(8,0));
draw((0,-8)--(0,8));
draw((-3,-8)--(-3,8),dashed);
draw((-8,3)--(8,3),dashed);
draw(graph(func,-8,-3.1),red);
draw(graph(func,-2.9,8),red);
filldraw(Circle((5,func(5)),0.15),white,red);

limits((-8,-8),(8,8),Crop);
[/asy]

The horizontal asymptote is \( y = 3 \) and the only vertical asymptote is \( x = -3 \). Find \( \frac{p(3)}{q(3)} \).

